          "summary": "Asks whether to revise the Danbury City Charter, as recommended by the Charter Revision Commission and approved by the City Council, so that all municipal elected offices (including Mayor, Town Clerk, Treasurer, City Council, Zoning Commission, Zoning Commission Alternates and Constable) have four-year terms starting with the November 2027 municipal election. It also revises Board of Education terms as set out in Section 2.2.A(c)(1) of the proposed revised charter.",
